  "scope": "Selected bind/skeleton and 90-degree shoulder/hip views of the exact generated Mirelle candidates, including focused joint screenshots; no full game-animation/contact qualification.",
  "observations": [
    "The inspected exact bind-pose silhouettes and foot positions remain consistent between the combined-pivot parent and the 12% weight-transfer candidate.",
    "Deep flexion still pinches shoulder/hip contact regions. The right hip transition has an angular crease in the close side view, and the shoulder-to-chest junction retains a visible notch/compression. Lower intersection counts do not establish a passing shape-quality gate.",
    "The separate diagnostic clip exports reproduce all 16 saved 45/90-degree bend counts for both candidates when sampled at normalized clip times. They are not game animation clips.",
    "Close-view rendering exposed a camera near-plane defect. The shipped Babylon inspector was repaired and the focused views repeated. The earlier blank-image run is rejected as visual evidence.",
    "Proceed with a 4mm spatial taper using the same 12% maximum transfer, donors, targets and parent. Preserve both existing candidates and record improvements and regressions before selection."
  ],
